GIT HISTORY — MinIO, AGPL-3.0

This repository's git history is not SeaweedFS's. Before 2026-06-19 this repo
held a fork of MinIO (github.com/minio/minio), and commit 466da88827 replaced
that code wholesale with the SeaweedFS engine while keeping the history. The
history root is MinIO's own first commit (397b887a87, 2014-10-30).

MinIO relicensed from Apache-2.0 to AGPL-3.0 in commit b2f907a47b
(2021-04-18, "update license change for MinIO"). Every commit from there
through 466da88827^ therefore contains AGPL-3.0 MinIO source, reachable by
checking out those revisions, in a repository whose current LICENSE is
Apache-2.0.

No AGPL-licensed code is present at HEAD, in any build, or in any published
artifact: the s3 binary, the module github.com/hanzoai/s3, and every released
image are built from the SeaweedFS-derived tree only. `grep` for the upstream
MinIO import path in the Go sources returns nothing. The exposure is confined
to historical revisions.

This is recorded rather than resolved. Truncating or rewriting the history
before the SeaweedFS import would remove it, at the cost of invalidating every
commit hash anyone has ever referenced; that is a decision about the
repository, not a metadata fix, and it is left open deliberately.

DEVIATIONS

  - Go module path renamed from github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs to
    github.com/hanzoai/s3. No residual upstream import paths remain in the Go
    sources.
  - Package tree relocated from the upstream weed/ directory to s3/; the CLI
    entrypoint is s3/s3.go.
  - Command binary renamed from weed to s3 (Makefile BINARY = s3); the CLI
    banner and subcommand descriptions are branded "Hanzo S3".
  - gRPC service identifiers renamed to Hanzo-prefixed names (for example
    HanzoClient, HanzoFilerClient, HanzoIdentityAccessManagementClient) under
    s3/wire/.
  - Versioning is independent of upstream's. Releases run on their own 1.0.x
    line (s3/util/version/constants.go) and no longer track upstream's 4.34.x
    numbering, so a version this binary reports does not name an upstream
    release.
  - SQLite is linked through github.com/hanzoai/sqlite, which registers the
    hanzoai/sqlcipher codec VFS; modernc.org/sqlite is present only as that
    module's dependency.
  - LICENSE preface augmented with a Hanzo AI, Inc. copyright line while
    preserving Chris Lu's copyright and the complete Apache-2.0 license text.
  - The S3-compatible object storage API under s3/s3api/ is retained as the
    primary product surface.
